(window.GROUP_QUIZZES=window.GROUP_QUIZZES||{})["pharmacology-i-exam-3-hf-inotropes-newer-agents-quiz"]={"title":"Other Heart Failure Drugs: Inotropes, Newer Agents & Aldosterone Antagonists Quiz 1 — Pharmacology I Exam 3","category":"Pharmacology I","exam":"Exam 3","sem":"fall-2026","questions":[{"q":"What does neprilysin inhibition do to myocardial tissue?","choices":["It inhibits growth and fibrosis","It promotes hypertrophy and fibrosis","It increases collagen deposition","It has no effect on tissue structure"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. Inhibiting neprilysin inhibits growth and fibrosis of myocardial tissue. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 81"},{"q":"What distinguishes the effect of ivabradine from that of a beta blocker?","choices":["It slows contractility but not the rate","It raises the rate and lowers contractility","It lowers both rate and contractility","It slows the rate but not contractility"],"answer":3,"exp":"Correct. Ivabradine reduces heart rate without affecting contractility, whereas beta blockers reduce both. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 79"},{"q":"A man taking spironolactone for heart failure develops breast enlargement. Which change to his therapy fits?","choices":["Add a loop diuretic","Add a potassium supplement","Switch to eplerenone","Stop all heart failure drugs"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. Eplerenone has far less androgen-receptor activity, so it rarely causes gynecomastia while keeping the aldosterone blockade. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 73"},{"q":"Which enzyme does sacubitril inhibit?","choices":["Angiotensin-converting enzyme","Phosphodiesterase 3","Neprilysin","Carbonic anhydrase"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. Sacubitril inhibits neprilysin, which normally degrades vasoactive peptides. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 81"},{"q":"Which cardiac adverse effect do milrinone and inamrinone share?","choices":["Symptomatic bradycardia","Ventricular arrhythmias","Complete heart block","Sinus arrest"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Ventricular arrhythmias are listed for these drugs. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 76"},{"q":"For which type of heart failure are sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitors used?","choices":["Acute decompensation with shock","Failure with severe low blood pressure","Stable, chronic reduced ejection fraction","Failure from advanced heart block"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. They are used in stable, chronic heart failure with reduced ejection fraction. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 82"},{"q":"Which finding makes ivabradine inappropriate?","choices":["A heart rate above 70","Heart block","Normal sinus rhythm","Maximal beta blocker therapy"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Ivabradine has contraindications like those of beta blockers: hypotension, heart block and a pacemaker. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 80"},{"q":"Which visual adverse effect is described for ivabradine?","choices":["Phosphenes","Xanthopsia","Cataract formation","Optic neuritis"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. Phosphenes are transient brightness in a limited area of the visual field, from effects on retinal photoreceptors. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 80"},{"q":"Which hematologic adverse effect do milrinone and inamrinone cause?","choices":["Megaloblastic anemia","Agranulocytosis","Thrombocytopenia","Polycythemia"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. Thrombocytopenia is the hematologic adverse effect listed for these phosphodiesterase 3 inhibitors. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 76"},{"q":"Which enzyme do milrinone and inamrinone inhibit?","choices":["Phosphodiesterase 5","Neprilysin","Sodium-potassium ATPase","Phosphodiesterase 3"],"answer":3,"exp":"Correct. They inhibit cyclic adenosine monophosphate phosphodiesterase 3, raising cyclic adenosine monophosphate in the heart and giving direct stimulation of contraction. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 74"},{"q":"How is dobutamine used in heart failure?","choices":["Short-term infusion to stabilize patients","Long-term oral maintenance therapy","Lifelong daily subcutaneous injection","A single dose to reverse toxicity"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. Dobutamine is given as a short-term intravenous infusion to stabilize patients. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 77"},{"q":"How do sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitors lower blood glucose?","choices":["The pancreas releases more insulin","The gut absorbs less glucose","The liver makes less glucose","The kidneys stop reabsorbing glucose"],"answer":3,"exp":"Correct. Blocking the sodium-glucose transporter means glucose is lost in the urine instead of reabsorbed. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 82"},{"q":"Which arrhythmia risk is increased by ivabradine?","choices":["Ventricular arrhythmias","Torsades de pointes","Atrial fibrillation","Asystole"],"answer":2,"exp":"Correct. Ivabradine increases the risk of atrial fibrillation, and it can also cause symptomatic bradycardia. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 80"},{"q":"Which laboratory finding makes a heart failure patient ineligible for spironolactone?","choices":["Potassium below 3.5 milliequivalents per liter","Potassium above 5 milliequivalents per liter","Sodium above 145 milliequivalents per liter","Chloride above 110 milliequivalents per liter"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Spironolactone holds on to potassium, so a potassium above 5 milliequivalents per liter excludes it, as does a high serum creatinine. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 73"},{"q":"Which risk comes with long-term use of milrinone or inamrinone?","choices":["Higher mortality and morbidity than placebo","Better survival with more edema","No difference from placebo","Slower progression of the disease"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. Long-term use is associated with higher mortality and morbidity than placebo, so use stays short term. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 76"},{"q":"Which infection risk rises with sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitors?","choices":["Bacterial pneumonia","Fungal urinary tract infection","Cytomegalovirus retinitis","Clostridioides difficile colitis"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Sugar in the urine promotes fungal growth, so fungal urinary tract infections are a unique adverse effect. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 82"},{"q":"What is the shortest washout advised when switching from an angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor to sacubitril-valsartan?","choices":["12 hours","6 hours","72 hours","36 hours"],"answer":3,"exp":"Correct. A 36 hour washout between the two drug classes avoids overlapping adverse effects. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 81"},{"q":"Which type of diuretic reduces mortality in advanced heart failure?","choices":["A loop diuretic","An aldosterone antagonist","A thiazide diuretic","A carbonic anhydrase inhibitor"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Spironolactone reduces mortality in advanced heart failure; the other diuretic classes relieve symptoms only. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 73"},{"q":"Which peptides does neprilysin normally degrade?","choices":["Aldosterone and cortisol","Epinephrine and norepinephrine","Renin and thrombin","Natriuretic peptide and bradykinin"],"answer":3,"exp":"Correct. Neprilysin degrades vasoactive peptides such as natriuretic peptide and bradykinin, which build up when it is inhibited. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 81"},{"q":"Why do sodium-glucose cotransporter 2 (SGLT2) inhibitors cause hypotension?","choices":["Fluid lost in urine lowers blood volume","They block beta-1 receptors in the heart","They dilate veins through nitric oxide","They inhibit neprilysin in vessels"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. The kidneys excrete extra glucose with fluid, so blood volume falls and blood pressure can drop. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 82"},{"q":"What does a dobutamine infusion increase more?","choices":["Rate of contraction more than force","Force of contraction more than rate","Venous tone more than force","Urine output more than force"],"answer":1,"exp":"Correct. Dobutamine stimulates the force of contraction more than the rate of contraction. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 77"},{"q":"Which outcomes does ivabradine reduce in heart failure?","choices":["Hospitalization and heart failure death","Blood pressure and sodium retention","Preload and afterload","Glucose and uric acid levels"],"answer":0,"exp":"Correct. Ivabradine has been shown to decrease hospitalization and heart failure related death. — Diuretics and Heart Failure Drugs.pptx, Slide 79"}]};
